    "result_text": "All rejection paths are now centralized. Let me summarize what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task required all rejection responses (400, 409, 429) to return an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`, with status codes unchanged.\n\n### What I found\n- **400** (bean-validation failures) already flowed through `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, whose `detailBuild` produces a `ProblemDetail` with all four members and `application/problem+json`.\n- **409/429** were emitted by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` as bare `new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT/TOO_MANY_REQUESTS)` \u2014 **no body at all**.\n- The provided acceptance test (`coreRejectionIsProblemJson`, removes `city`, expects **400**) actually returned **500**: `CityRegionTable.regionOf(null)` calls `Map.of(...).getOrDefault(null, ...)`, and immutable maps throw NPE on a null key. So a missing required field crashed instead of being rejected cleanly.\n\n### Changes\n1. **`CityRegionTable.regionOf`** \u2014 treat a null city as \"not in the table\" \u2192 `UNKNOWN`, matching its documented contract. Removes the NPE so a missing city is reported as a clean 400 by the existing validation.\n2. **New exception hierarchy** in `rest/advice`: an abstract `RestApiException` carrying an `HttpStatus` + detail, and three concrete rejections \u2014 `CityAtCapacityException` (409), `DuplicateOwnerException` (409), `DailyRegistrationLimitException` (429). Each has a single responsibility: signal *what* was rejected, not shape the body.\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleRestApiException`** \u2014 one handler that reuses the existing `detailBuild` to render any `RestApiException` as problem+json at its carried status, keeping error-body construction in one place alongside the other rejection handlers.\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 the three bare-status returns now `throw` the corresponding exceptions, so the controller stays focused on the happy path and rejections get consistent problem+json bodies.\n\n### Verification\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, all tests green (the acceptance test now gets 400 + `application/problem+json` + `$.status == 400`). A grep confirmed the owner controller was the only site emitting domain 400/409/429, so coverage is complete.",
